  "preamble": "The Middle Chinese voiced alveolo-palatal affricate [dʑ] of the 常/禪 initial became the plain voiceless fricative [s] in Cantonese and Hakka in all tones, losing voicing, affrication and palatality together. Mandarin instead has retroflex [ʂ] for the same etyma, with [ʈʂʰ] in level-tone words such as 常 cháng; the 船 initial, reconstructed as the fricative [ʑ], also gives Cantonese [s].",
